Task 2: Spring Boot – BLOB Storage Using JPA
Repository
Scenario
Build a Spring Boot application for a Digital Archive System that stores scanned certificates as
binary data in the database.
Entity Class: ArchiveDocument
Fields:- Long documentId- String documentTitle- String ownerName- String fileType- byte[] documentData (@Lob)
Requirements:
1. Create the ArchiveDocument entity.
2. Annotate documentData with @Lob to store it as a BLOB.
3. Create an ArchiveDocumentRepository extending JpaRepository<ArchiveDocument, Long>.
4. Implement: Save file, Retrieve by ID, Update binary file, Delete, Display metadata.
5. Insert at least 3 sample records.
6. Verify retrieved BLOB can be written back to a file.
7. Test using CommandLineRunner or REST APIs.
Expected Learning:- @Lob for BLOB storage- Binary file handling in Java- JpaRepository- CRUD on large objects- Reading/writing files with byte[]